-- title:
--   Descent of the formal group law along invariant coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $B$ a commutative Noetherian ring. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$ in the sense of the project structure `FormalODModule`, so that in particular $X$ carries a two-dimensional formal group law $X.F$ over $B$, a commutative one, together with a $\mathbb{Z}_p^2$-action and a uniformiser series satisfying the stated compatibilities. Let $I$ be an ideal of $B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]=\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\;2)\;B$ such that the quotient $B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/I$ is finite and projective as a $B$-module. Let $u=(u_0,u_1)$ be a pair of power series in two variables, each with zero constant term, subject to two conditions. Invariance: for each $j$, the difference $u_j(X.F(x,y))-u_j(x)$, formed in $B[\![x,y]\!]$ with $x$ the `Sum.inl` and $y$ the `Sum.inr` variables, lies in the ideal generated by the image of $I$ under substitution of the $y$-variables. Parametric descent: for every $n$ and every $w\in B[\![x_0,x_1,t_1,\dots,t_n]\!]$ such that $w(X.F(x,y),t)-w(x,t)$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $I$ in the $y$-variables, there is a unique $W\in B[\![x_0,x_1,t_1,\dots,t_n]\!]$ with $W(u(x),t)=w$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a two-dimensional formal group law $G$ over $B$ (zero constant terms, prescribed linear terms, associativity) which is commutative and for which $u$ is a homomorphism of laws from $X.F$ to $G$: the $u_i$ have zero constant term and $u_i(X.F(x,y))=G_i(u(x),u(y))$ for each $i$.
--
--   This is the descent step in the construction of the quotient of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module by a finite subgroup, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: invariant coordinates $u$ that are coordinates on the quotient in the parametric sense carry the group law of $X$ down to a commutative formal group law for which $u$ is an isogeny of laws. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates), and relies on a projectivity criterion for membership in ideals generated by substituted series.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_exists_mvFormalGroup_isComm_isLawHom_of_invariant_coordinates.lean

